      "title": "The application server must generate log records for access and authentication events.",
      "description": "Log records can be generated from various components within the application server.  From an application server perspective, certain specific application server functionalities may be logged as well.  The application server must allow the definition of what events are to be logged.  As conditions change, the number and types of events to be logged may change, and the application server must be able to facilitate these changes.\n\nThe minimum list of logged events should be those pertaining to system startup and shutdown, system access, and system authentication events.",
